{"agent_id":"driver","agent_seq":41,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T03:21:20.709483011Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c66a4338-cef5-44fa-bc52-a2230b30f5eb","comment_uuid":"01691f58-871c-481a-a066-214012d71684","author":"driver","content":"Result: review fixes committed as 4efd9ae6 (ASES #192, [#798]). 1) MAJOR: ensure_worktree_heartbeat renamed ensure_worktree_hooks — now writes .claude/hooks/crosslink_config.py from CROSSLINK_CONFIG_PY alongside heartbeat.py when either is missing (best-effort); new subprocess regression test executes the real heartbeat.py in a fresh-worktree layout with fake crosslink shim on PATH, proving import succeeds and last-heartbeat is written AND updated. 2) MINOR: new stall_marker_path(worktree_dir, crosslink_dir) helper reads watchdog.stall_marker via read_watchdog_config (default .kickoff-stalled); threaded into status + discover_agents; unit-tested for default+custom. 3) MINOR: hook-config.qmd watchdog section rewritten to evidence-recorder semantics (never kills/nudges, terminal-sentinel exit per #138), documents watchdog.stall_marker + kickoff.timeout_backstop_secs (default max(timeout*24,24h)); --timeout help in main.rs (Run/Plan/Launch) + embedded kickoff.md/SKILL.md updated to guide semantics (NOT killed). 4) NIT: vacuous {worktree} assertion removed. 5) NIT: docker --stop-timeout comment corrected (sets grace for later docker stop; does not self-trigger); value unchanged. Tests: kickoff::tests 193/193 PASS, full bin compiles (--no-run), clippy no NEW warnings (only pre-existing launch.rs:74 + main.rs:3414). No push/install/live-kickoff.","created_at":"2026-08-06T03:21:20.702823367Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:cx5PuRP0j7pktPKktl0WwbMp5uEwfFy9WoiBcgyhe18","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguEQKo5PmNONBqYSfFi6Ry6tvLy9D5GLM9YcPkF7QNdoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAxlgJAC+ndD6bFWt4IleZiBOOKh71a0Q5Fp0mKpfTzhD5rYsuOw8xIA2Enc5EDC6QTPVMeBFs3YGqJghFeS/UDw