{"agent_id":"driver","agent_seq":44,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T03:28:45.061422993Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c66a4338-cef5-44fa-bc52-a2230b30f5eb","comment_uuid":"e9e531c1-1ebc-411e-8eda-5d412176f1a2","author":"driver","content":"Verdict: APPROVE-WITH-NITS\n\nRe-review basis: commit 4efd9ae6 on feature/ases-192-timeout-backstop (fix commit only; core 0e014c45 previously reviewed, no-kill contract found correct). Verified by full diff read, tracing heartbeat.py guard clauses and find_crosslink_binary, tracing stall_marker writer/reader paths, running kickoff tests, running clippy.\n\nFinding-by-finding (all 5 prior findings):\n1. MAJOR (heartbeat hook dependency) - FIXED. launch.rs:583-601: ensure_worktree_hooks now writes BOTH crosslink_config.py (from CROSSLINK_CONFIG_PY, init/mod.rs:37-38, same include_str resource init uses) and heartbeat.py when either is missing. Regression test test_heartbeat_hook_runs_and_writes_stamp_after_ensure_worktree_hooks (tests.rs:2964-3064) is HONEST, not vacuous: it builds a fresh-worktree layout, satisfies heartbeat.py guard clauses (hook-config.json + agent.json in wt/.crosslink, traced against resources/claude/hooks/heartbeat.py:42-63), puts a fake crosslink shim first on PATH (shutil.which resolves it), executes the REAL heartbeat.py via python3 subprocess, and asserts (a) exit 0 (crosslink_config import does NOT crash - would fail under old single-file write), (b) .crosslink/.cache/last-heartbeat written with content, (c) shim actually invoked (log polled up to 2s, de-racing Popen), (d) after touch -t aging, second run UPDATES the stamp mtime (<60s old). Passes in isolation and in the suite. Not trivially passing.\n\n2. MINOR (stall_marker config sync) - FIXED. launch.rs:131-137: stall_marker_path(worktree_dir, crosslink_dir) reads read_watchdog_config(crosslink_dir).stall_marker with .kickoff-stalled fallback (empty-string markers filtered, launch.rs:110-114). monitor.rs:154 (status) and monitor.rs:266 (discover_agents) both USE it. Test test_stall_marker_path_default_and_custom (tests.rs:2745-2773) covers default + custom and asserts they differ.\n\n3. MINOR (docs drift) - FIXED. hook-config.qmd:134-147 documents kickoff.timeout_backstop_secs (default max(timeout*24, 86400), 0 = default - matches read_backstop_override *v>0 filter, launch.rs:53); watchdog section (qmd:197-240) rewritten as pure evidence recorder (never kills/nudges, terminal-sentinel exit by status CONTENT, stall marker surfaced); max_nudges marked DEPRECATED (matches tolerant read, launch.rs:92-99; script never uses it); watchdog.stall_marker documented, KICKOFF_EXCLUDE_PATTERNS claim verified (helpers.rs:406). main.rs --timeout help in all 3 spots (Run/Plan/Launch) + kickoff.md/SKILL.md now say guide semantics (NOT killed at timeout, backstop only guards a wedged process) - accurate, not overpromising.\n\n4. NIT (vacuous assertion) - FIXED. The !script.contains literal-placeholder assertion is removed from test_build_watchdog_script_contains_key_elements; the positive DONE*|FAILED*|CI_FAILED*|TIMEOUT* content assertion (tests.rs:2797-2800) plus no-send-keys/no-nudge negatives remain.\n\n5. NIT (docker --stop-timeout comment) - FIXED. launch.rs:874-881: comment now correctly states --stop-timeout does NOT self-trigger (only sets SIGTERM grace for later user-invoked docker stop); destroyer guard is the timeout backstop wrapper inside the container. Value unchanged (consistent with prior review's acceptance).\n\nNew findings:\n1. NIT - main.rs:1674-1675 (and ~1754-1756, ~1832-1834): the last two lines of each new --timeout doc comment are not indented (start at column 0) while the rest of the doc block is 8-space indented. Purely cosmetic - /// lines are contiguous so clap help text concatenates correctly and compilation is unaffected. Re-indent for style. Not blocking.\n\nAdditional checks:\n- Scope discipline: 4efd9ae6 touches exactly the 7 expected files. No out-of-scope edits. main.rs changes are wording-only doc comments in the 3 --timeout spots - no logic changes.\n- Stall-marker worktree consistency: NO BUG. Watchdog writer (launch.rs:801, read_watchdog_config(crosslink_dir)) and readers (monitor.rs:154/266) resolve from the SAME crosslink_dir (find_crosslink_dir from invoking cwd = main repo .crosslink normally). hook-config.json is a tracked committed file (.gitignore:59-61), so a worktree's committed copy is normally identical. Running status from INSIDE a worktree would resolve that worktree's .crosslink first - pre-existing find_crosslink_dir behavior (main.rs:2217-2252), identical before this fix; not a regression.\n- Contract re-check (no-kill invariant after fix commit): HOLDS. Changed lines contain no kill paths: stall_marker_path is read-only; ensure_worktree_hooks only writes hook files (best-effort); monitor changes are read-only marker checks; main.rs is doc comments; tests are test-only. Watchdog script still only exits 0 on terminal status content or session-gone and writes the marker (launch.rs:158-190); only autonomous destroyer remains the documented generous timeout backstop. Kill paths (kickoff stop, cleanup, container stop/kill) are user-invoked, unchanged.\n- No NEW clippy warnings in changed files: 24 warnings all pre-existing (launch.rs:74 empty_line_after_doc_comments from commit 8a207fffd 2026-07-11, not this commit; main.rs:3414 is SentinelCommands, outside changed region).\n\nTests run:\n- cargo test --bin crosslink kickoff::tests: 193 passed, 0 failed (4.42s). Includes all new tests (heartbeat hook functional run, stall_marker default+custom, ensure_worktree_hooks write/config/preserve).\n- Single-run of the heartbeat functional regression test: passes (real python3 + heartbeat.py + fake shim executed).\n- cargo clippy --bin crosslink: compiles clean, no new warnings in changed files.\n- Full 2862-test suite not run (previous review found it infra-bound); kickoff::tests is the targeted scope and is green.\n\nBottom line: all 5 prior findings are genuinely fixed, verified in code, tests, and runtime-path tracing. The only residual issue is a cosmetic doc-comment indent NIT. Approving.","created_at":"2026-08-06T03:28:45.054399397Z","kind":"verdict","signed_by":"SHA256:cx5PuRP0j7pktPKktl0WwbMp5uEwfFy9WoiBcgyhe18","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguEQKo5PmNONBqYSfFi6Ry6tvLy9D5GLM9YcPkF7QNdoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAf58Rr+rHzP1OO6QKmA0UN2aOcdVVM1gyahrb8oG4XZdyRuFd/l6YkjioCqAIpkMHG3S9d2JsDXPdt8Te+bslDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:cx5PuRP0j7pktPKktl0WwbMp5uEwfFy9WoiBcgyhe18","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguEQKo5PmNONBqYSfFi6Ry6tvLy9D5GLM9YcPkF7QNdoAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOgbrjeU1r1+ogle7u9OKMVZhj8vUY3OSmwaJlQZobxrZtSeKb9yk9Wmxkr2Y13k41jEELgtASHjvzkmcXxJ6AM="}
